# `core::primitives::valueless` -- `void` and `never`, the two built-ins
# with no values at all: nothing to construct, store, compare or pass, and
# neither is conformable since a spec method needs a `self` to receive.

# The absence of a value, not an empty one. A function's "returns nothing";
# occupies no storage.
primitive void { }

# The bottom type: what an expression has when control never reaches past
# it. Legal only as a function/method/extern/gap declared return type; this
# declaration site is the one exception to never being a binding/field/
# parameter type.
primitive never { }
